---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { webPageSchema, schemaScript } from '../lib/seo';
import type { BreadcrumbEntry } from '../lib/seo';

const breadcrumbs: BreadcrumbEntry[] = [{ name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy' }];
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Paula Ambrosio Interiors collects, uses and protects information submitted through this website."
	canonical="/privacy"
>
	<Fragment slot="head" set:html={schemaScript(webPageSchema({
		path: '/privacy',
		title: 'Privacy Policy | Paula Ambrosio Interiors',
		description: 'Privacy policy for the Paula Ambrosio Interiors website.',
		breadcrumbs,
	}))} />

	<article class="container-editorial max-w-3xl pt-16 pb-24 lg:pt-24">
		<Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
		<h1 class="font-display mt-10 text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-mist">
			Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-08">October 8, 2026</time>
		</p>

		<div class="prose-editorial mt-12">
			<h2>Information you send us</h2>
			<p>
				The inquiry forms on this website ask for your name, email address, telephone number,
				project location, property type, the service you are interested in, an approximate
				budget, your desired timeline and a short description of your project. Only your name,
				email address, project location, service and message are required; the remaining fields
				help us prepare for the first conversation and are entirely optional.
			</p>
			<h2>How your inquiry travels</h2>
			<p>
				When you send an inquiry, the form is processed by our website's own server, not by a
				third-party form service and not by your email client, and delivered as an email to
				<a href="mailto:info@paulaambrosio.com">info@paulaambrosio.com</a>. If the inquiry reaches
				us, you also receive a confirmation email at the address you provided. We keep your
				message in our mailbox and in our project records. Our website does not manually send
				inquiry messages to advertising services; the optional OpenAI Pixel behavior is described below.
			</p>
			<h2>How information is used</h2>
			<p>
				Inquiry information is used to answer your message, schedule consultations and
				communicate about a potential project. We do not sell your personal information, and we
				do not share it with third parties for their own marketing.
			</p>
			<h2>Service providers</h2>
			<p>
				This website is hosted by Vercel, which processes requests, including form submissions,
				on our behalf. Email is delivered through the mailbox provider that hosts
				info@paulaambrosio.com. Both act as service providers under our instructions and receive
				only what is required to deliver the service.
			</p>
			<h2>Analytics and performance data</h2>
			<p>
				We use Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights to understand which pages are
				visited, broadly where visitors come from and how the site performs on real devices.
				These reports are aggregated and do not build advertising profiles. The contents of an inquiry (your name, contact details
				and message) are never included in that data; we only record which page a form was sent
				from and which service was selected.
			</p>
			<h2>Optional Google tools and your consent</h2>
			<p>
				Our Privacy choices control offers separate, optional choices for website analytics and
				advertising measurement. Both are off until you choose them. Google Tag Manager loads
				only after you allow at least one category. Loading it sends Google a network request,
				which includes technical connection information such as your IP address and browser information.
				Google Analytics 4 runs only when you allow website analytics. Google Ads measurement,
				remarketing and lead-conversion reporting remain paused.
			</p>
			<p>
				Analytics measures visits to public pages and selected interactions with our services and
				website controls. Google may use analytics cookies and technical identifiers and process
				device, browser and approximate geographic information to produce these reports.
				We do not send names,
				email addresses, telephone numbers, inquiry messages or other contact-form fields to these
				Google tools. Automatic collection of user-provided contact data, Google Signals, enhanced
				conversions and personalized advertising are not enabled. An interaction or form attempt
				is not recorded as proof of an accepted or qualified lead.
				See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for how Google handles data.
			</p>
			<p>
				We save only your optional-tool choices and their date in this browser. Your choices are
				valid for up to 90 days before we ask again.
				You can reject or change them through Privacy choices without losing access to our forms.
				Withdrawing permission immediately stops our site from sending further measurement events
				and attempts to remove first-party Google measurement cookies. If tools have already loaded,
				we offer a reload after you finish your form to unload them. Previously sent data is not undone
				by changing your browser choices.
			</p>
			<h2>Optional OpenAI advertising measurement</h2>
			<p>
				If you allow Advertising measurement in Privacy choices, we load the OpenAI Pixel.
				The request shares technical connection information, including your IP address and browser
				information, with OpenAI. The Pixel may use first-party cookies and advertising click or
				browser identifiers for attribution. Its __oppref cookie can last up to 30 days and its
				__obref cookie up to 365 days, subject to your browser's restrictions.
			</p>
			<p>
				We do not manually supply contact details, hashes of contact details, budgets or inquiry
				messages to the Pixel. Depending on the Pixel's account settings, OpenAI's automatic advanced
				matching may detect supported contact information entered on this site and hash it in your
				browser for conversion matching. We have not verified that this automatic matching is disabled.
				Hashing does not make this information anonymous. This site currently installs only the base
				Pixel and does not send lead-created conversion events.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Pixel is not loaded before advertising permission is granted. Withdrawing permission
				instructs the Pixel to stop measurement and removes its first-party attribution cookies.
				Reload after finishing your form to unload code already loaded; previously transmitted data
				cannot be recalled by changing these choices. See
				<a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI's Privacy Policy</a> and
				<a href="https://developers.openai.com/ads/measurement-pixel">OpenAI's Pixel documentation</a>.
			</p>
			<h2>Security</h2>
			<p>
				All traffic to this site uses HTTPS. Email credentials live only on our server and are
				never sent to the browser. Submissions are validated on the server and protected against
				automated abuse.
			</p>
			<h2>Your choices</h2>
			<p>
				You may ask us to correct or delete the information you have sent us at any time. Write to
				<a href="mailto:info@paulaambrosio.com">info@paulaambrosio.com</a> and we will remove it
				from our records, except where we are required to keep it for accounting or legal
				reasons.
			</p>
			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any privacy question, contact
				<a href="mailto:info@paulaambrosio.com">info@paulaambrosio.com</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
